From: CatOS Package Maintainers <packages@catos.info>
Subject: [PATCH] build: do not embed the package build directory

The source-tree fallback is only useful for an uninstalled development build.
A distribution binary must not retain the absolute package build directory, so
use the installed assets directory for the fallback as well.

---
 meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 3db7adb..f17a8ad 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -207,5 +207,5 @@ executable('noctalia-greeter',
     '-Wall', '-Wextra', '-Wpedantic', '-Wconversion', '-Wshadow',
     '-DNOCTALIA_GREETER_VERSION="' + meson.project_version() + '"',
-    '-DNOCTALIA_GREETER_ASSETS_DIR="' + meson.project_source_root() / 'assets' + '"',
+    '-DNOCTALIA_GREETER_ASSETS_DIR="' + get_option('prefix') / get_option('datadir') / 'noctalia-greeter' / 'assets' + '"',
     '-DNOCTALIA_GREETER_INSTALLED_ASSETS_DIR="' + get_option('datadir') / 'noctalia-greeter' / 'assets' + '"',
   ],
